# Bentoo — locale set for the built image. FIXED and versioned here.
#
# This file is the single source of truth for which locales glibc compiles.
# It is NEVER read from the build host: image content must not depend on the
# operator's machine (LAB-NOTES D2/F4). Changing the language set is a
# deliberate edit to this file, not a side effect of where the build ran.
#
# Note: this is distinct from L10N in make.conf. L10N picks which package
# translations get installed; this picks which glibc locales exist at all.
#
# Cost: 102 locales -> ~78 MB of /usr/lib/locale/locale-archive.

# This file defines which locales to incorporate into the glibc locale archive.
# See the locale.gen(5) and locale-gen(8) man pages for more details.

